@host = http://localhost:5103

### 1. Not signed in: expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/suppliers

### 2. Sign in as the requester
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "requester@vivabev.example", "password": "Demo@2026!" }

### 3. Who am I? Note the permissions list
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### 4. Reading suppliers is allowed: expect 200
# @name list
GET {{host}}/api/suppliers?status=pendingapproval

###
@pendingId = {{list.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 5. Approving is not: expect 403
POST {{host}}/api/suppliers/{{pendingId}}/approve

### 6. Switch to the procurement manager
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

###
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "procurement.manager@vivabev.example", "password": "Demo@2026!" }

### 7. Now approval works: expect 204
POST {{host}}/api/suppliers/{{pendingId}}/approve

### 8. Wrong password five times locks the account (try it on the buyer)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "buyer@vivabev.example", "password": "wrong-password" }
